{
  "$comment": [
    "Editorial romanization preferences for Ukrainian.",
    "",
    "Applied BEFORE the transliteration scheme. Anything not matched here falls",
    "through to the scheme (KMU 2010 by default), so this file holds only the",
    "cases where a standard and editorial practice disagree.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  forms       Cyrillic surface forms. Ukrainian declines and English does",
    "              not, so every inflected form maps to one invariant output.",
    "  declension  Optional. 'adj' expands a -ський/-ний stem across its cases.",
    "  latin       What the archive publishes.",
    "  gloss       Optional English meaning, where usage translates rather than",
    "              romanizes.",
    "  note        Why the entry exists. This file is an editorial record; the",
    "              reasoning belongs beside the decision.",
    "",
    "Place-name spellings here are Ukrainian-derived, not Russian-derived.",
    "That is a deliberate editorial position, not a transliteration artefact."
  ],

